  "description": "NEZSEU crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I 41/a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C24 H56 Cl6 Gd4 Mn2 O17. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.058-5.026 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 83.87-173.29°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C24H56Cl6Gd4Mn2O17. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ6-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
